---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
import config from "../../site.config.mjs";
import { phases, plans } from "../data/onboarding.mjs";
// The onboarding page (docs/product/client-journey.md, B-04): how a platform becomes a client, phase by phase.
// Six phases on the site, with no shadow phase (founder, 2026-11-28). There is no free pre-sale report.
---
<Base title="Onboarding" description={`How a platform becomes a ${config.brandName} client: six phases from discovery to scale, each with an owner and an exit check you sign.`}>
  <PageHead title="Onboarding in six phases." lead="From the first call to every rail. Each phase has an owner on both sides and an exit check, and you sign every step that moves money closer to being sent.">
    <div class="ctas" data-reveal><a class="button" href="/access/">Request access</a></div>
    <Fragment slot="fragments">
      <div class="frag" data-ui data-reveal><p class="frag-title">Phase 4 · Policy setup</p>
        <p>Rule set v1, versioned</p><span class="chip st-READY">SIGNED OFF</span><p class="soft">By your compliance lead.</p></div>
      <div class="frag" data-ui data-reveal><p class="frag-title">Phase 5 · Go-live</p>
        <p>Assist → Auto on one rail</p><span class="chip st-ESCALATED">YOUR SIGN-OFF</span><p class="soft">Kill-switch owner and backup owners named first.</p></div>
      <div class="frag" data-ui data-reveal><p class="frag-title">Sample data</p>
        <p>Every figure on this page is an example.</p></div>
    </Fragment>
  </PageHead>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap">
    <Prose>
      {phases.map((p) => (
        <>
          <h2 data-reveal>{p.n}. {p.name}</h2>
          <div class="block" data-reveal>
            <p>{p.what}</p>
            <p><strong>We own:</strong> {p.us}. <strong>You own:</strong> {p.you}.</p>
            <p><strong>{p.sign ? "You sign:" : "Exit check:"}</strong> {p.exit}.</p>
          </div>
        </>
      ))}
      <h2 data-reveal>Your data</h2>
      <div class="block" data-reveal>
        <p>The contract and a data processing agreement are signed before any of your data reaches us. Data is hosted in a UK or EU region and used only as the agreement sets out. The agreement names every region and every subprocessor.</p>
        <p><strong>By phase.</strong> Discovery and contract use only the business details you choose to share. In the sandbox, use the fictional counterparties and test values, not your customers' data. Your live payment data reaches us from go-live onward, under the agreement.</p>
        <p><strong>What we keep.</strong> Every decision and change is kept in an append-only, hash-chained audit trail, and any decision can be replayed. Sandbox request logs are kept for 30 days; other sandbox data until your evaluation organisation expires, plus 30 days. Retention of live data is set in the data processing agreement.</p>
        <p><strong>What we never hold.</strong> Client funds or keys.</p>
      </div>
      <h2 data-reveal>Plans</h2>
      <div class="block" data-reveal>
        <p>The Pilot covers phases 3 to 5 on one rail. {plans.join(", ")} are a software fee per payment decided, never a share of the money you move. <a class="textlink" href={`mailto:${config.salesInbox}`}>Talk to us</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </Prose>
  </div></section>
</Base>
<style>.ctas { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap; }</style>
